      {
        "title": {
          "en": "Enterprise AI Value Focus Shifts to Operating Layer",
          "zh": "企业AI价值重心转向运营层"
        },
        "tl_dr": {
          "en": "While public discourse centers on foundation models and benchmarks, the lasting advantage in enterprise AI lies in owning the operating layer where intelligence is applied and governed.",
          "zh": "尽管公众关注基础模型和基准测试，但企业AI的持久优势在于拥有智能应用和管理的运营层。"
        },
        "key_takeaways": {
          "en": [
            "Public discourse on enterprise AI primarily tracks foundation models and benchmarks.",
            "Key benchmarks discussed include reasoning scores and marginal capability gains of models such as GPT and Gemini.",
            "The structural advantage in enterprise AI is found in owning the operating layer, which governs intelligence application and improvement."
          ],
          "zh": [
            "企业AI的公众讨论主要围绕基础模型和基准测试展开。",
            "讨论的关键基准包括GPT和Gemini等模型的推理分数及边际能力提升。",
            "企业AI的结构性优势在于拥有运营层，该层负责管理智能的应用与改进。"
          ]
        },
        "impact": {
          "en": "This perspective suggests that the long-term competitive landscape in enterprise AI will be defined by control over the integration and management of AI systems, rather than solely by model performance. This reorients focus from raw model capabilities to the strategic deployment and governance infrastructure.",
          "zh": "这一观点表明，企业AI的长期竞争格局将由对AI系统集成和管理的控制权决定，而非仅仅是模型性能。这使得行业焦点从原始模型能力转向战略部署和治理基础设施。"
        },
        "source": "MIT Tech Review",
        "link": "https://www.technologyreview.com/2026/04/16/1135554/treating-enterprise-ai-as-an-operating-layer/"
      }
